Bootstrap Chain Milestones
==========================

Version  Milestone
-------  ---------
00       Minimal DATA-only bootstrap (129 bytes)
01       First non-standard 6502 mnemonics
02       Source becomes human-readable assembly
03       Byte selectors, label assignments, origin setting
05       Two-pass assembly (forward references)
07       Instruction table generator (instgen)
10       .include directive
11       First modularized source
16       Standard 6502 syntax support
17       Source transitions to standard syntax
18       Forward reference tracking
19       Expression evaluation
20       .ifdef/.endif conditional assembly
22       Macros
23       Self-hosting, .ifndef/.else


Source Syntax Evolution
=======================
Each version's source can only use syntax supported by the version that
builds it. The left column shows new syntax each version can assemble;
the right column shows new syntax first used in that version's source.

Ver New syntax supported             New syntax used in source
--- -------------------------------- ----------------------------
00  DATA $XX, ; comments             -
01  Non-standard mnemonics           None
    (LDA#, STAZ), labels,
    strings, $XXXX hex
02  None                             Non-standard mnemonics,
                                     labels, label references
03  < > byte selectors,              Char escape literals
    label = $XX, * = $XXXX
04  None                             = assignments, < > selectors
05  Two-pass (fwd refs),             * = origin
    ~ branches, more instrs
06  None                             None
07  More instrs (via instgen),       None
    flag-based operand types
08  None                             ZP addressing without <
                                     (STAZ VAR not STAZ <VAR)
09  None                             None
10  .include                         None
11  More instructions                .include
12  .zeropage, .code                 None
13  None                             .zeropage, .code
14  Local labels (.prefix)           None
15  None                             Local labels (.prefix)
16  Standard 6502 syntax,            None
    all 13 addr modes, #'x'
17  None                             Standard 6502 syntax,
                                     #'x' character literals
18  .data directive                  None
19  Expressions (+, -),              .data (replaces DATA)
    char lits as terms
20  .ifdef/.endif, define:           Expressions (+, -),
                                     char literal arithmetic
21  .macro/.endmacro, << >>,         .ifdef/.endif, define:
    optional label colons
22  .byte/.word/.asciiz/.reserve,    Colons, macros, << >>
    decimal, comma-separated
23  .ifndef, .else                   .byte, .word, .asciiz,
                                     decimal constants
